  "question": {
    "text": "A fully charged capacitor $C$ with initial charge $q_0$ is connected to a coil of self inductance $L$ at $t=0$. The time at which the energy is stored equally between the electric and the magnetic field is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Vuul4",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\sqrt{L C}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "hpEKv",
      "text": "\n$2 \\pi \\sqrt{L C}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l9DWz",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{L C}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0Xpjx",
      "text": "\n$\\pi \\sqrt{L C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Charge oscillates simple harmonic motion $q=q_0 \\sin \\omega t, U=\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{q^2}{C}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& q=\\frac{q_0}{\\sqrt{2}} \\Rightarrow \\omega t=\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow t=\\frac{T}{8}=\\frac{2 \\pi}{8} \\sqrt{L C}=\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\sqrt{L C}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
